# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in what you need. Both the Next app and
# the collector scripts read it — bun loads .env.local automatically.
#
# Nothing here is required to run the app. `bun run export` builds
# data/skolregister-export.json, and the app reads that file on its own.


# --- Bolagsverket ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# Required by `bun run koncern bygg` and nothing else. Bolagsverket's API needs
# a key; Skolverket's does not, so `bun run export` and `bun run build` work
# without these. Read in bolagsverket.ts, and only ever server-side — the
# secret must never reach a client bundle.
#
# Without them, `bun run koncern bygg` fails with a message naming these two
# variables rather than a bare 401.

# BOLAGSVERKET_KLIENT_ID=
# BOLAGSVERKET_HEMLIGHET=

# "produktion" (default) or "test" for the acceptance environment, which has
# its own separate keys. Note the non-ASCII Ö.
# BOLAGSVERKET_MILJÖ=produktion


# --- Register data: overrides, not requirements ---------------------------
#
# The app reads data/skolregister-export.json when it exists — that is what
# `bun run export` writes, and no configuration is involved. Set this only to
# read an export from somewhere else. See registerFilePath() in
# src/lib/skolregister/client.ts.

# SKOLREGISTER_DATA_FILE=/absolute/path/to/some-other-export.json

# Fallback for when there is no export file at all: the app then reads the API
# served by `bun run api` (server.ts). Note that server defaults to port 3000,
# the same port `bun run dev` uses — start it on another port, or the app will
# be talking to itself and every list will come back empty.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3001


# --- The collector's own server -------------------------------------------
#
# Port for `bun run api`. Read in server.ts.

# PORT=3001
